Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.28,0:00:19.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,So today um I'm going to talk about uh robot learning from human experience uh and
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.07,0:00:26.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,how scale uh is starting to change uh what robots can learn and how they learn.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.80,0:00:30.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'll frame the talk around uh three hypotheses.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.75,0:00:41.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so first robot capabilities can scale with human data and second human data will soon be unabundant uh to be sufficient enough to
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.36,0:00:51.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,the point where we don't know how to do about it and third progress requires scaling the both the science uh uh and the data.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.06,0:00:53.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,So they are the hypothesis not facts.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.04,0:01:01.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh but I hope this talk will provide some evidence uh that concrete evidence uh that they are becoming true.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.92,0:01:08.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,I hope I have I don't have to convince you that robot learning have made a lot of progress and one of the key factors
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.32,0:01:15.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,is that we have rediscovered tele operation to be a really good way to teach robot how to do really complex tasks like making laundryries,
